  ],
  "notes": "Measured on F-OTOA's left side (LAX, 2026-03-22) fitted to the 787-9 shape by its doors (residuals 10–30 px, about 0.5–1 m along the body); checked against its right side (LAX, 2026-03-07), which has the same layout (stripes, motif field, arcs, chevron bands) with its own motifs: areas apply to both sides, so the right side is the left's pattern, its chevrons and spirals not checked one by one. The tattoo panel is our own simplification, not a trace of the artwork: three slanting turquoise stripes and a chevron band (widths and slant measured at two rows), then a turquoise field divided into cells by three blue bands at the photo's measured gaps, each cell carrying a tidy blue spiral above and below the windows; the artwork's motifs themselves stay the THT/tattoo logo's. Behind it, the tail's arcs (a wide turquoise arc round door 4, a turquoise band with a row of blue chevrons sweeping down and aft, a thin arc under the tailplane, one under the fin and a ring round the tail cone) and the fin's bands (top trailing corner, chevron band, two plain bands, a thin arc from the lower leading edge to the root) were measured point by point on the left photo through the fit. Each aircraft's name (TETIAROA, etc.) is lettered small under the flag, not drawn. The 787's raked wingtips carry no winglet paint.",
  "history": "New file (Air Tahiti Nui had no scheme here). The 787-9s (from 2018) introduced this scheme; the earlier A340 scheme (white with blue-green tail) has left the fleet."
}